direct, `failwith`, formatted, `@@`, quantified, `p_all2`, `pf`, and short refusal formats are extracted: true
comments, quoted code, and a dynamic value contribute no diagnostic string constant: true
Printf substitutions are holes and a stable literal fragment becomes the fragment: true
an absent fragment is an orphan: true
the diagnostic's unique marker in a control golden covers it: true
two diagnostics sharing a display fragment still require distinct controls: true
one control marker occurrence covers only one identical diagnostic: true
one observed claim execution is consumed by only one matching diagnostic: true
a second identical diagnostic cannot reuse the consumed claim execution: true
a row holding the extraction in order has no difference: true
a reworded format is one marker added and one removed, with no order to report: true
a row holding the same markers in another order names the first misplaced entry: true
a direct failure new to the row, observed by nothing, is named for a direct-evidence entry; a new claim is not: true
a second occurrence of a listed direct failure is new to the row, and is named: true
a direct failure the row already lists asks for no new evidence: true
a passed control claim and the refusal's line from a refused run exercise it: true
a passed control claim alone, with no refused run printing the refusal, does not: true
a refused run printing a different refusal does not either: true
the refusal's line alone, with the mapped claim not passed, does not: true
the refusal's line from a run ANOTHER passed claim made does not, beside the mapped claim's runs: true
while the same line from the mapped claim's own run does: true
an observation from the caught branch exercises it with no mapping: true
a line a more specific sibling format also matches does not exercise the general one: true
the general refusal's own line still exercises it beside the specific sibling: true
and the specific sibling owns the line both formats match: true
a catalogue-only refusal nothing executes stays catalogue-only: true
a catalogue-only refusal a refused child run prints is reported as executed: true
and so is one its caught branch observes: true
a manifest source missing from the argument list is named as uncatalogued: true
an argument-list source outside the manifest is named as extra: true
a source catalogued twice is a mismatch, not a match: true
a manifest row repeated is a mismatch even where the argument list repeats it too: true
the same sources in another order match: true
the stanza's scanner sources are exactly Refusal_control_manifest.sources, each once: true

